-- title:
--   A k₀-form F₀ of the full-level field, case q=3
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=3$, a level $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over the residue field of $A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with the geometric $j$-value in the supersingular set), let $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of the former along $A$ onto $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ whose residue map is computed coefficientwise on Laurent series with coefficients in $A$. Further data: an index $\zeta\in\mathrm{Idx}\,q$, a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by the projective line over $\mathbb{Z}/q$ and a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$, subject to: the explicit description of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ as the set of $f$ admitting a representation $f\cdot y=x$ with $x,y$ Laurent series over $A$ and $y$ of non-zero reduction; transitivity of the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ under pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ together with $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma\cdot\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q=\ell$; injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; permutation of the family by pullback along every $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$; the conditions that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ meets $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in $A$, is stable under all these level automorphisms, contains an element $t$ with $t-a$ a unit for every $a\in A$, and receives the $R_0$-integral functions $f$ (those with $\mathrm{ord}_P f\ge 0$ whenever $\mathrm{ord}_P$ of the image of $j$ is $\ge 0$) whose $R_0$-residue is $s$-integral, with $f-a$ in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ when $\mathrm{residue}\,A\,a=s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,f)$; a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ on $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}$ at level $q^2M'$ with subgroup $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ whose ring of integers is $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$, and the identification of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$; an element $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$. Finally, small-constant data: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $A\cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, every element of $A$ being congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$; and tame data: a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$, $\ell\nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and $\varpi_t\in k_0\cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. The conclusion asserts, for the $k_0$-algebra structure on $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ induced from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the existence of an intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ such that: the $k_0$-subfield generated by $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with $F_0$ is everything; $F_0$ is mapped into itself by $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; $F_0$ is regular over $k_0$ in the form that for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ finite over $k_0$, every finite family $c_i\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a_i$ in the subfield generated by $K'$ and $F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$; and every element of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ whose Laurent expansion has rational coefficients lies in $F_0$.
--
--   This is the construction, on the Igusa branch of the semistable covering of the full-level modular curve at $q=3$, of a model over the small field $k_0$ of the geometric function field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(q^2M'))$: a $k_0$-form $F_0$ which generates the whole field together with the constants, is stable under the level automorphisms coming from $\Gamma_0(M')$, is regular over $k_0$, and contains all functions with rational $q$-expansion. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_three) in the construction of the Igusa base model and its smooth-point stalks; the statement is the $q=3$ counterpart of the corresponding result for $q\ge 5$.
